Introduction to the PHP class constants #

	- Sometimes, you need to define a constant that is specific to a class. In this case, you can use the PHP class constants.


		class Circle
		{
		    const PI = M_PI;
		}

	- Since a constant is defined per class, not per instance of the class, you use the self keyword to reference the constant inside the class

	-  you can use visibility modifier keywords such as private, protected, and public with the class constant. For example:


	class Circle
	{
	    private const PI = M_PI;

	    // other methods   
	}


